{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_io2qs7diduc6itf3sbkdqpke3pnr5l4zmrb6pw7lnfyeyhvod7xa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four phases complete. Summary:\n\n**Phase A — builds.** C: `cd c_src/build && cmake .. && cmake --build .` → `c_src/build/driver`. Rust: `cd translation && cargo build --release` → `translation/target/release/driver`. Both built clean; **no compile errors needed fixing**.\n\n**Phase B/C — differential tests.** `translation/tests/differential.rs` (19 tests) spawns both binaries as subprocesses, pipes identical stdin, and asserts **stdout, stderr and exit status** all match. The C is 12 lines of logic (`scanf(\"%lf\")` → `printf(\"%llx %a %.4f\\n\")`), so the branch space is entirely in libc's scanf/printf. I enumerated 18 input classes from it and covered each: empty/EOF, whitespace-only, matching failure, plain decimals, exponent forms and the *backtracking* cases (`1.5e`, `0e+`, `0x1p-`), `inf`/`infinity` plus every partial-match failure (`in`, `infi`, `infinit`), `nan`/`-nan`/`nan(...)`, hex floats, `0x` with no digits vs `0x.`, overflow, underflow, subnormals, trailing input, and non-UTF-8/NUL bytes. Plus systematic sweeps: all 104 single-bit subnormals, trailing-zero significands at all 53 nibble positions, ~1200 random bit patterns as exact hex literals, ~1200 random decimals, ~1200 over-long hex significands (sticky-bit path), 2000 random garbage strings, and full walks of the exponent boundaries.\n\n**Result: zero mismatches** across ~22,000 probes (19 tests plus ad-hoc sweeps). The translation was already correct; nothing in `translation/src/main.rs` needed changing.\n\n**Phase D gate — verified with my own commands, not self-reports:**\n- clean rebuild from scratch (deleted `c_src/build` and `translation/target`) succeeds for both\n- `cargo test` → 19 passed, 0 failed, **0 ignored**; `grep -c` for `#[ignore]` in `tests/` → **0**\n- `cargo test --release` also passes (19/19)\n- `c_src/` sources unmodified — sha256 of `CMakeLists.txt` and `src/main.c`; only the generated `build/` dir was touched\n- the suite self-builds the C program if `c_src/build/driver` is absent (verified by deleting it and re-running)\n\n`translation/ERRORS.md` records the C behaviour table, the \"no mismatches found\" result with the full probe inventory, and — since there were no failures to log — the 12 specific divergence hazards I checked and the named test guarding each (e.g. exit status must stay 0 on parse failure; `scanf` skips newlines so a line-based reader would break; `-0` must keep its sign bit in `%llx`; `-nan` must print as `-nan`, which Rust's native formatting won't do; `%.4f` ties round to even).\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: this verification pins the Rust output to **glibc's** scanf/printf as built on this machine. The `%a` and NaN-sign behaviours it depends on are glibc-specific, so the same tests run against a musl or BSD libc build of the C could legitimately diverge."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2072,"cache_read_input_tokens":50902,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2072,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af48adf1-bea3-42d5-ba93-b8922a3fe9c8","uuid":"54f2d315-3ce5-40a3-845c-a7af202392b9","timestamp":"2026-08-28T16:59:27.512Z"}
